<title>SRI LANKA: Ceylon Brewery up on foreign buying.</title>
<headline>Ceylon Brewery up on foreign buying.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ceylon Brewery Ltd rose 2.3 percent, or 75 cents, to 33.75 rupees, on foreign buying of 225,000 shares, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We had to bid up to tempt sellers and get this quantity,&quot; said a broker at CT Smith Stock Brokers.</p>
<p>The company is the main brewer in Sri Lanka which also brews Carlsberg and Guinness under licence.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
